//Problem: To Lower Case
//Approach: String class in Java has a built-in method toLowerCase() which converts all the characters in the string to lower case. We can simply call this method on the input string and return the result.
//Time Complexity: O(n), where n is the length of the input string. We need to iterate through each character in the string to convert it to lower case.
//Space Complexity: O(n), where n is the length of the input string. The toLowerCase() method creates a new string with the converted characters, which requires additional space.
//Difficulty: Easy

class Solution {
    public String toLowerCase(String s) {
        return s.toLowerCase();
    }
}